 "findings": [
  "Raising Jev's threshold is the lever: held out, 0.5 wrongly blocks 282 of 2,432, 0.98 blocks 1, 0.99 blocks 0.",
  "The stricter question lost catches without losing wrong blocks, so the gate's question stays.",
  "Requiring two or three guards to agree never beat Jev alone at the same number of wrong blocks.",
  "DeBERTa's scores sit near 0 or 1: it wrongly blocks 483 of 2,997 even at 0.995.",
  "Laya has no threshold with near-zero wrong blocks on all sets with any question tried; it needs fine-tuning.",
  "Several of Jev's wrong blocks at 0.95 contain explicit override text; the benchmark calls them benign because the request inside is harmless."
 ],
 "next": [
  "Review band: pass 0.5 to 0.98 but flag it",
  "A second Jev question about harm, block when both are sure",
  "Fine-tune Laya or DeBERTa on real benign traffic and attacks"
 ],
